    "content": "### The Monsoon Challenge\nIn India, the rainy season brings relief from heat but also creates breeding grounds for mosquitoes carrying Dengue, Malaria, and Chikungunya.\n\n### Preventive Measures\n- **Clear Stagnant Water**: Check pots, coolers, buckets, and terraces weekly. Standing water is where Aedes and Anopheles mosquitoes lay eggs.\n- **Mosquito Nets & Repellents**: Use DEET-based repellents during the day and mosquito nets at night.\n- **Full Clothing**: Wear light-colored, long-sleeve shirts and full trousers when stepping outdoors.\n\n### Symptom Checklist\nWatch out for the following:\n- Sudden high fever (up to 104°F)\n- Severe joint and muscle pain (often called \"break-bone fever\" for Dengue)\n- Pain behind the eyes\n- Rashes and mild bleeding (nose/gums)\n\nIf you experience these symptoms, avoid taking pain relievers like Aspirin or Ibuprofen, which can worsen bleeding. Take Paracetamol and seek immediate professional medical attention."
